    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0543" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg531"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.11 E.W. International Telephone and Telegraph
                    Corporation/8–2245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Czechoslovakia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Praha</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-22T19:00:00+02:00">August 22, 1945—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>244. Notwithstanding the assurances the Embassy received from Zecho Minister of
                    Foreign Affairs<anchor n="64" xml:id="d524-f1"/> that plant of C. Lorenz, A. G.
                    located at Vrchlabi Zecho had been removed from official list of war booty
                    plants, we are now reliably informed that Russians are preparing to remove 75
                    percent of equipment for shipment to Russia,<anchor n="65" xml:id="d524-f2"/>
                    This <pb facs="0544" n="532" xml:id="pg532"/> plant is property of International
                    Tel and Tel Co. We have made further representations to Zecho Government on
                    subject but suggest Department bring matter to attention Russian Government
                    before equipment is removed.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept as 244, repeated Moscow as 29.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d524-f1" n="64" xml:id="d524-f1-content">
                <p>Jan Masaryk.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d524-f2" n="65" xml:id="d524-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 103, September 11, 6 p.m. to Vienna, reported that Col. Sosthenes Behn,
                    President of the International Telephone and Telegraph Corporation, had been in
                    Prague recently where he heard unofficially that the Soviet Government had put
                    the Vrchlabi vacuum tube factory back on the war booty list and proposed that 75
                    percent of plant’s machinery and material would be moved to the Soviet Union
                    (360F.115 International Telephone and Telegraph Corporation/9–1145).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
